{"format":"tvf-scene","v":1,"name":"example · the Tangent Bridge","loop":30,"ease":"inout","hold":0,"gravity":1,"wind":0,"trail":null,"camera":[{"t":0,"box":[-0.431977036,0.00244134861,-0.0471943301,0.340840786]},{"t":0.62,"box":[-0.431977036,0.00244134861,-0.0471943301,0.340840786]},{"t":0.68,"box":[-0.258843361,0.00156039076,-0.000727901745,0.334105862]},{"t":0.76,"box":[-0.258843361,0.00156039076,-0.000727901745,0.334105862]},{"t":0.8,"box":[-0.431977036,0.00244134861,-0.0471943301,0.340840786]}],"stops":[0.14,0.3,0.48,0.62,0.76],"beats":[{"title":"A curve is a function on the circle","text":"Seen from its middle, a closed shape is one distance for every direction: a function *F* on the circle. This one has a little detail in it, waves of three, five and nine to a turn.\n\nThe theorem asks two questions about it. What do you have to keep of *F*, and what do you get back?"},{"title":"Read it at the atoms","text":"Read *F* in eight directions, evenly spaced, at the odd multiples of π/8. **Eight numbers are kept, and nothing else.**\n\nEach reading is taken on its own, in a fixed amount of work. None of them needs to know how many others there are, or what lies between. In the paper these directions are the *atoms*; in a .tvf file they are the leaves. [The forward map, §3](../papers.html#tb_classical:3.1-definition)"},{"title":"One kernel, turned to every atom","text":"To give the readings back as a curve, each one carries the same shape: the kernel K₈(φ) = sin 4φ ⁄ (8 tan ½φ).\n\nIt is **1 at its own atom and 0 at every other**. Here the bright petal touches the base circle exactly where the other seven rays cross it. The faint ones are the same kernel, turned to the other atoms. [The kernel, §4.2](../papers.html#tb_classical:4.2-kernel-properties)"},{"title":"Their sum passes through every atom","text":"Weight each kernel by its reading and add them up. The result is the violet curve.\n\nAt an atom only that atom's kernel is nonzero, so the sum there **is the reading, exactly**. Read the curve back in the eight directions and you get the eight numbers you started with, to the last digit. These are (R1) and (R2) of the theorem. [The statement, §5.1](../papers.html#tb_classical:5.1-statement)"},{"title":"Between the atoms: close, and bounded","text":"Between two atoms the curve is the kernels' best guess. Eight readings cannot hold waves of five and nine to a turn, so those come back as slower waves, and here, at the widest gap, the curve misses *F* by about 28 on a radius near 100.\n\nThe miss is never unbounded. It is at most a constant, times log *N*, times how far *F* itself moves within one atom's spacing (R3). A smooth *F* is missed by little, a rough one by more. [Bounded between, §6.3](../papers.html#tb_classical:6.3-r3-bounded-between)"},{"title":"Double the atoms, and the curve closes in","text":"With sixteen atoms, each of the eight slides half a step and eight more come in between them; with thirty-two, sixteen more. The lattice doubles, and the doubling map θ ↦ 2θ carries each lattice onto the one before.\n\nThe violet curve closes in on *F*. Thirty-two atoms hold every wave of fewer than sixteen to a turn, and the finest wave of *F* is nine, so at thirty-two **the curve is *F* exactly**. For any *F* smooth enough the curve converges as the atoms double (R4). At no step did the reading or the sum use anything but the readings themselves (R5). [Convergence, §6.4](../papers.html#tb_classical:6.4-r4-convergence-and-the-necessity-of-the-class)"}],"path":null,"items":[{"fill":{"color":"#f4f1ea","opacity":1},"stroke":null,"width":0,"open":false,"exact":{"x":[-0.9,0.9,0.9,-0.9],"y":[0.675,0.675,-0.675,-0.675],"r":null,"smooth":null,"ctrl":null,"holes":[]}},{"morph":42},{"morph":0},{"morph":2},{"morph":3},{"morph":4},{"morph":5},{"morph":6},{"morph":7},{"morph":8},{"morph":9},{"morph":10},{"morph":11},{"morph":12},{"morph":13},{"morph":14},{"morph":15},{"morph":16},{"morph":17},{"morph":43},{"morph":45},{"morph":46},{"morph":47},{"morph":48},{"morph":49},{"morph":50},{"morph":51},{"morph":52},{"morph":18},{"morph":19},{"morph":20},{"morph":21},{"morph":22},{"morph":23},{"morph":24},{"morph":25},{"morph":26},{"morph":27},{"morph":28},{"morph":29},{"morph":30},{"morph":31},{"morph":32},{"morph":33},{"morph":34},{"morph":35},{"morph":36},{"morph":37},{"morph":38},{"morph":39},{"morph":40},{"morph":41},{"morph":53},{"morph":54},{"morph":55},{"morph":56},{"morph":57},{"morph":58},{"morph":59},{"morph":60},{"morph":61},{"morph":62},{"morph":63},{"morph":64},{"morph":65},{"morph":66},{"morph":1},{"morph":44},{"morph":67}],"morphs":[{"exact":true,"open":false,"holes":null,"keys":[{"x":[-0.0856308642,-0.0912742481,-0.100252925,-0.110568276,-0.120151944,-0.127484929,-0.132007666,-0.134186363,-0.135230542,-0.136584355,-0.139390856,-0.144126172,-0.150523138,-0.157784805,-0.164975932,-0.171419429,-0.176936702,-0.181847554,-0.186752228,-0.192209566,-0.198463452,-0.205340583,-0.212360743,-0.219002959,-0.225000047,-0.230520645,-0.236147537,-0.2426519,-0.250655437,-0.260325744,-0.271240728,-0.282488603,-0.292969909,-0.301779917,-0.308511973,-0.313352435,-0.316924524,-0.319946047,-0.322848923,-0.325530597,-0.327357161,-0.327434233,-0.325046125,-0.320084791,-0.313281789,-0.30612532,-0.300464931,-0.297931665,-0.29938098,-0.304566708,-0.312174379,-0.320211243,-0.326618701,-0.329891353,-0.329487023,-0.325893014,-0.320343572,-0.31431108,-0.308970224,-0.304832017,-0.301667293,-0.298720048,-0.295098756,-0.29017263,-0.283811759,-0.276386811,-0.268550854,-0.260917287,-0.253786051,-0.24704116,-0.24026073,-0.232982884,-0.225000046,-0.216540717,-0.208247547,-0.20095132,-0.195332835,-0.191618019,-0.189442099,-0.187949343,-0.18609485,-0.183026714,-0.178389146,-0.172417189,-0.165780367,-0.1592402,-0.153269554,-0.14780387,-0.14224413,-0.13572758,-0.127566768,-0.117678366,-0.106815032,-0.0964823529,-0.0885434775,-0.0846392049],"y":[0.168749929,0.17751478,0.185173199,0.191511824,0.196843896,0.201851854,0.207268637,0.2